  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/307F33">Example <span data-tag="307F33">7.3.4.6</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a presentable $\infty $-category in which filtered colimits are left exact, and let $\calD \subseteq \calC $ be the essential image of an (accessible) left exact localization functor $L$. Then filtered colimits in $\calD $ are left exact. To prove this, we consider an arbitrary filtered $\infty $-category $\calI $, and observe that the colimit functor $\varinjlim : \Fun (\calI , \calD ) \rightarrow \calD $ is equivalent to the composition </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Fun (\calI , \calD ) \subseteq \Fun (\calI ,\calC ) \rightarrow \calC \stackrel{L}{\rightarrow } \calD , \]
</div>
  <p> where the second arrow is given by the colimit functor $\varinjlim \Fun (\calI ,\calC ) \rightarrow \calC $. </p>
</article>